{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they shall know.</b> Rabbi Judah the first grammarian already mentioned the distinction between וְיָדְעוּ and וְיֵדְעוּ: for the kamatz in kamatz gadol is past tense, like שׁׂמְעוּ, and the vav converted it to future as is the rule; and the kamatz in kamatz katan, and the yod is a sign of future, like וְיִשְׁמְרוּ, and leave hidden what is between the yod and the dalet—the yod is a root letter. Now he stated why He brought the plagues upon the Egyptians: so that His revered name be known in the world."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:19.098697669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}